From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0001/0014] Rebrand product.json

This patch rebrands the application metadata in product.json.

Rationale: the fork ships as Jahaziel Code with its own protocol, data
folders, bundle identifiers, license, and issue tracker.

Touches:
  - product.json (all nameShort, nameLong, applicationName, dataFolderName,
    urlProtocol, serverApplicationName, serverDataFolderName, win32*,
    darwinBundleIdentifier, licenseName, licenseUrl, reportIssueUrl fields)

Target product.json:
  {
    "nameShort": "Jahaziel Code",
    "nameLong": "Jahaziel Code",
    "applicationName": "jahaziel-code",
    "dataFolderName": ".jahaziel-code",
    "urlProtocol": "jahaziel-code",
    "serverApplicationName": "jahaziel-code-server",
    "serverDataFolderName": ".jahaziel-code-server",
    "win32MutexName": "jahazielcode",
    "win32DirName": "Jahaziel Code",
    "win32NameVersion": "Jahaziel Code",
    "win32RegValueName": "JahazielCode",
    "win32AppUserModelId": "Jahaziel.Code",
    "win32ShellNameShort": "Jahaziel Code",
    "darwinBundleIdentifier": "dev.jahaziel.code",
    "licenseName": "MIT",
    "licenseUrl": "https://github.com/jahaziel-project/jahaziel/blob/main/LICENSE",
    "reportIssueUrl": "https://github.com/jahaziel-project/jahaziel/issues/new",
    "quality": "stable"
  }

Diff: authored on the upstream checkout (see build.sh).
Verification: smoke test opens with Jahaziel Code branding.
